# RETIRED SCAFFOLD SOURCE (SN-028). This dial now lives in
# process.toml.template -> docs/process.toml as `[policies] blackout`, and
# bootstrap.py no longer copies this file into a new repo — shipping both
# homes would hand every scaffold the mixed-config refusal. The file stays
# in the kit as the reference for the legacy vocabulary that
# `bootstrap.py --migrate-config` reads when converting an existing
# adoption; the text below describes that legacy home, not today's.
#
# Blackout window (process-options.md "Unattended operation"). One value on the
# last line — a UTC weekday (Mon–Fri) window the coordinator starts NO new
# session inside:
#   HH:MM-HH:MM   — a 24-hour UTC window; an in-flight session wraps normally,
#                   then the loop waits the window out and resumes automatically
#                   (a single walk-away launch survives the blackout).
#   start == end  — disabled (e.g. 00:00-00:00); so is deleting this file
#                   (absent = disabled, byte-identical to a repo that never had
#                   it). A window whose start is after its end wraps past
#                   midnight.
# The half-open window [start, end) blocks `start` through the minute before
# `end` and releases at `end`. Change this value in a reviewed commit, like
# docs/gate. The default below pauses new sessions during weekday working hours.
12:00-19:00
